+Custom Card Identification
+==========================
+
+The optional ``cid`` property sets the 128-bit card identification register.
+Provide exactly 32 hexadecimal characters, without a ``0x`` prefix or spaces.
+Both uppercase and lowercase are accepted. When omitted, the existing QEMU
+identity is used. This property is specific to eMMC and does not change SD cards.
+For example, add the following property to the eMMC device:
+
+.. code-block:: console
+
+    -device emmc,drive=emmc-img,cid=15010043494431323310012345672900
+
+The value is reapplied on device reset. Configure the same value on migration
+endpoints; the existing CID migration state is unchanged. Changing CID does not
+modify the backing image. A realized device's CID property cannot be changed.
+
+SDHCI omits the final CRC/end-bit byte from its 136-bit response registers.
+Consequently Linux's ``/sys/block/mmcblk0/device/cid`` reports that last byte as
+``00``, regardless of the property's last two hexadecimal characters. The other
+15 bytes match the configured value. Values copied from Linux sysfs can be used
+directly, including their final ``00``; QEMU does not validate or regenerate the
+CRC byte of a custom CID.
